# Guard against publishing project files that live outside site/.
# Only the site/ folder should ever be deployed, so these paths shouldn't
# exist on a live site. If they're uploaded by mistake, these rules hide them.
#
# Netlify honours these rules. Cloudflare Pages does NOT support 404 rules in
# _redirects and skips them; there, publishing only site/ is the protection.
/.git/*          /404.html   404!
/README.md       /404.html   404!
/CHANGELOG.md    /404.html   404!
/docs/*          /404.html   404!
/tests/*         /404.html   404!
/screenshots/*   /404.html   404!
